   "he": "עוֹשֶׂה אָדָם תַּבְשִׁיל מֵעֶרֶב יוֹם טוֹב. אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא תַּבְשִׁיל, אֲבָל פַּת — לָא.",
   "en": "It was taught in the mishna that «a person may prepare a cooked dish on a Festival eve» and rely on it for Shabbat for the joining of cooked foods. «Abaye said: They taught» that the joining of cooked foods allows one to cook on a Festival for Shabbat «only» when it is made from «a cooked dish; however,» if it is composed of «bread» alone, «no,» this is not sufficient."
  }
